          <h3 class="table-heading">Kids' US to Mexico Shoe Size Chart</h3>
          <div class="table-wrapper">
            <table class="size-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>US Kids Size</th>
                  <th>Mexico Talla (CM)</th>
                  <th>Inches</th>
                  <th>EU Size</th>
                  <th>UK Size</th>
                  <th>Stage</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {kidsSizes.map(r => (
                  <tr>
                    <td class="primary-cell"><strong>US {r.us}</strong></td>
                    <td class="highlight-cell"><strong>MX {r.mx}</strong></td>
                    <td>{r.inch}″</td>
                    <td>EU {r.eu}</td>
                    <td>UK {r.uk}</td>
                    <td>{r.stage}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Editorial Guide -->
    <section class="editorial-band">
      <div class="page-inner prose-article">
        <h2 class="editorial-main-title">The Complete US to Mexico Shoe Sizing Guide: Punto Calzado, Cowboy Boots &amp; Formulas</h2>

        <p class="lead-paragraph">
          Whether you are traveling to Mexico, purchasing authentic leather cowboy boots from the shoemaking capital of León, Guanajuato, or shopping cross-border online, understanding <strong>american shoe size to mexico</strong> conversion is essential. Because Mexico utilizes the metric <em>Punto Calzado</em> system alongside colloquial numbering conventions, learning the exact formulas ensures you achieve a flawless fit.
        </p>

        <h3>1. How Mexican Shoe Sizing Works: The Punto Calzado Standard</h3>
        <p>
          Unlike the United States, which measures footwear in imperial barleycorns (1/3 of an inch), official Mexican footwear sizing is based directly on foot length in centimetres. In Mexico, footwear measurement is officially designated as <strong>Punto Calzado</strong> (or simply <em>Puntos</em>), where each punto corresponds to one centimetre (CM).
        </p>
        <p>
          A shoe marked as "Punto 27" or "Talla 27" indicates that the shoe last was sculpted for an anatomical foot length of exactly 27.0 centimetres. Because centimetres represent a static physical unit, calculating your <strong>shoe size in mexico</strong> eliminates ambiguous scale shifts.
        </p>

        <h3>2. Men's Conversion: Subtracting 1.5 from US Sizing (`Mexico ≈ US − 1.5`)</h3>
        <p>
          For men, <strong>convert shoe size us to mexico</strong> by subtracting approximately 1.5 sizes from your standard American shoe size:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>US 7 to Mexico</strong> = MX 5.5 (approx. 25.0 cm foot length)</li>
          <li><strong>US 8 to Mexico</strong> = MX 6.5 (approx. 26.0 cm foot length)</li>
          <li><strong>US 9 to Mexico</strong> = MX 7.5 (approx. 27.0 cm foot length)</li>
          <li><strong>US 9.5 to Mexico</strong> = MX 8.0 (the popular <strong>mexico shoe size to us size</strong> benchmark for 27.5 cm)</li>
          <li><strong>US 10 to Mexico</strong> = MX 8.5 (approx. 28.0 cm foot length)</li>
          <li><strong>US 10.5 to Mexico</strong> = MX 9.0 (approx. 28.5 cm foot length)</li>
          <li><strong>US 11 to Mexico</strong> = MX 9.5 (approx. 29.0 cm foot length)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This offset represents the mathematical bridge between American imperial lasts and Mexican metric footbeds.
        </p>

        <h3>3. Women's Conversion: Subtracting 3.0 from US Sizing (`Mexico ≈ US − 3.0`)</h3>
        <p>
          In women's footwear, American sizing begins further down the scale. To calculate <strong>mexican to us shoe sizes</strong> for women, subtract approximately 3.0 sizes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>US 5 Women</strong> = Mexico 2.0 (Punto 22.0 cm)</li>
          <li><strong>US 6 Women</strong> = Mexico 3.0 (Punto 23.0 cm)</li>
          <li><strong>US 7 Women</strong> = Mexico 4.0 (Punto 24.0 cm)</li>
          <li><strong>US 8 Women</strong> = Mexico 5.0 (Punto 25.0 cm)</li>
          <li><strong>US 9 Women</strong> = Mexico 6.0 (Punto 26.0 cm)</li>
          <li><strong>US 10 Women</strong> = Mexico 7.0 (Punto 27.0 cm)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          In Mexican boutique footwear stores, women's shoes are often labeled directly with their centimetre footbed length (e.g., "24 cm" instead of "Talla 4").
        </p>

        <h3>4. The Dropped-Digit Convention: "Talla 7" vs "Talla 27"</h3>
        <p>
          A common source of confusion for international shoppers looking at <strong>shoes sizes mexico usa</strong> is the dropped-digit naming convention. In everyday Mexican commerce, vendors and retail staff frequently drop the leading digit "2":
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Punto 28 cm</strong> is colloquially known as <strong>Talla 8</strong> (or <em>size 8 en Mexico</em>).</li>
          <li><strong>Punto 27 cm</strong> is called <strong>Talla 7</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Punto 26.5 cm</strong> is called <strong>Talla 6.5</strong> or <strong>6 y medio</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Whether a shoe box is stamped "28" or "8", both indicate the exact same 28.0 centimetre last.
        </p>

        <h3>5. Handcrafted Boots from León: Cuadra, Flexi, and Western Lasts</h3>
        <p>
          León, Guanajuato produces a massive share of the world's finest handcrafted leather western boots. Renowned Mexican bootmakers—such as <strong>Cuadra, Los Altos, Flexi, and Franco Cuadra</strong>—utilize traditional cowhide, ostrich, and caiman leathers built over structured wooden lasts.
        </p>
        <p>
          When shopping for authentic Mexican cowboy boots:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Pointed Toe Shapes (Snip / J-Toe):</strong> Because pointed toe profiles taper sharply at the front, your toes will sit further back in the shoe cavity. US buyers with average or wide feet should order a half-size larger than their measured Mexican size to allow adequate forefoot clearance.</li>
          <li><strong>Instep Fit:</strong> Traditional cowboy boots feature no laces; the boot is held on your foot entirely by the instep fit. A new Mexican boot should feel snug across the instep with slight heel slip (about 1/4 inch) before breaking in and molding to your foot.</li>
          <li><strong>Flexi Casual Shoes:</strong> Flexi brand casual shoes and loafers fit true to metric length and offer generous forefoot width, making them ideal for standard daily wear.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>6. Cross-Border Buying Tips: Measuring Foot Length for US &amp; Mexican Sizing</h3>
        <p>
          When navigating <strong>conversion shoe size mexico to us</strong> or looking up <strong>shoe size from usa to mexico</strong>, taking a physical foot measurement in centimeters provides the ultimate reassurance. To ensure seamless shopping:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Trace Your Bare Foot:</strong> Place a blank sheet of paper against a flat wall, stand with your heel touching the wall, and mark the outermost tip of your longest toe. Measure the distance in centimeters to get your exact <em>Punto</em> number.</li>
          <li><strong>Check the Label Format:</strong> On imported boots sold in Texas, California, and online, size tags often list both sizes (e.g., "US 9.5 / MEX 8.0"). If only one number appears on a Mexican-made shoe and it is between 22 and 31, it is almost certainly the Mexican Punto length in centimeters.</li>
          <li><strong>Account for Sock Thickness:</strong> Western boot socks are typically thicker than dress socks. Factor in approximately 0.5 cm of extra space if you intend to wear heavy winter or work socks.</li>
        </ul>
